ype":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[This](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108242#issuecomment-3048909721) comment suggested a possible confusion between native abstract classes, and abstract scripts. Native abstract classes cannot be extended from by scripts, but abstract scripts can (at least abstract GDScript classes). I was concerned that introducing further ambiguity would only increase confusion.\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\n\r\nIn my experience, it is often better to have something communicate intent rather than behaviour (especially where behaviour is the direct result of intent). That is what I was hoping to do here. While the only difference right now is in connection to abstract scripts, this might not be true into the future.\r\n\r\nIf we wanted to avoid using an enum (because it only has 2 states after all, so it *is* overkill) I would think that `bool for_inheritance` might be clearer. Another solution might be to create a new class (`InheritDialog` maybe) that internally sets any appropriate behaviour flags (rather than simply re-purposing the `CreateDialog`). Or still have the method be something like `for_inherit` that similarly sets any/all internal behaviour flags.\r\n\r\n(These are just my views and thoughts. I am responding to what I read as a query for my views and reasoning. I respect your views as a maintainer, and I will change the PR if you say that I should. I am not attempting to argue.)","created_at":"2025-08-04T20:48:25Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T22:44:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109203#discussion_r2252554409","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109203","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2252554409"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109203#discussion_r2252554409"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109203"}},"reactions":{"u